Status: Pending. Owner refinement, 2026-11-22: prove the complete electronic object through real library, construction, instrument, firmware and coupled-device implementations.

[Development graph](../Workspace-Development.lingua) · [Electronics workbench contracts](../contracts/Electronics-workbench-contracts.lingua)

## Start gate and ownership

Require verified exports from Electronic Libraries, Electronic Prototyping, Electronics Workbench, Mixed Signal Circuits, Firmware Devices and Electromechanical Devices, plus full 11a and 15a acceptance. This planned numerical integration is not a prerequisite for existing core or base 15a acceptance. Earlier providers close their independent proofs before this join; reopen them only for a discovered defect or an explicitly owned extension.

Own the late composition adapters and EB acceptance evidence. Shared result, instrument, clock, model and command changes remain coordinated with their existing owners, one writer at a time. Do not create another instrument runtime or scheduler. Pin the bounded combined fixture, mappings, backend versions, tolerances and resource limits before implementation.

## Ordered work

### Task EBI.T01

- [ ] Import ELB's actual supported model package, inspect and repair a deliberate terminal-order mismatch, then execute its reference manifest through MSG's admitted evaluator. Confirm source/version/units and independent expected electrical outputs; parsing and metadata inspection cannot satisfy numerical validation. Build EPT's real prototype, power its extracted net graph, and observe supply/open-return consequences through EWB. Cross-probe component/pin/contact/net identities into the intended schematic and 11a's corresponding PCB realization. Preserve opens/shorts as discrepancies instead of rewriting design intent. Package a supported subcircuit with exposed ports, parameters, retained internals and its experiment; prove two independent instances.

### Task EBI.T02

- [ ] Connect real mixed-signal and firmware event observations to the existing instrument channels. Implement triggered bounded digital capture, an actual VCD writer and one actual I²C decoder, selected and pinned with the fixture. Independently inspect the exported transitions and decoded known transactions; map each result to source pins, firmware identity, run clock and validity. Test short pulses, unknown/high-impedance values, malformed transactions and truncated capture. Preserve bounded pre/post-trigger retention and explicit missing coverage. These late adapters do not delay EWB's earlier analog measurements or numeric export.

### Task EBI.T03

- [ ] Compose the proved firmware, declared sensor input and electromechanical load in the named prototype using actual supported GPIO/PWM/driver bridges. Show a changed input changing firmware output and motor response; load changes must affect current/back-EMF through the validated coupling. Keep protocol, electrical and mechanical observations separately identified. Check independent timing and energy references. Replay 15a's already validated detailed/cheap stateful transition on its own named pair while unrelated functional content continues. No motor/firmware transition is inferred from that proof; unsupported state transfer remains unavailable or requires the declared restart.

### Task EBI.T04

- [ ] Complete EB.W01–EB.W07 and EB.P01/EB.P02 through native controls, mapping each to EB.R01–EB.R14 and actual provider evidence. Exercise cross-view selection, offline package reopening, restricted hosted observation, source rights, missing dependencies, stale edits, cancellation at synchronization boundaries and authority loss. Preserve per-instance memory and one output writer. Verify edit-panel geometry, focus and reachable controls. Measure setup, simulated-time throughput, event/sample/instruction counts, coupling error, peak resources and final release with fixed observables. Retain unchanged provider evidence; record composition defects and their owning repairs.

## Completion

Publish implemented late adapters, exact supported formats/decoder, independent references, native replay, measured bounds and remaining unsupported scope. Close the Electronics workbench contract only after the actual combined workflows pass. Current outcome: unbuilt and unverified.
